# App Routes

## Route groups

| Group | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `(marketing)/` | Public landing |
| `(auth)/` | Login, register — client forms + Better Auth client |
| `(app)/` | Authenticated shell — `AppShell`, `ensureUserContexts` |
| `api/` | Route handlers — JSON only |

## Auth

- Middleware checks `better-auth.session_token` cookie for protected paths
- Server pages: `requireSession()` from `@/infrastructure/auth/session`
- API routes: `getServerSession()` → 401 if missing
- Client auth actions: `@/infrastructure/auth/client`

## API handler pattern

```typescript
export async function POST(request: Request) {
  const session = await getServerSession();
  if (!session) return NextResponse.json({ error: "Unauthorized" }, { status: 401 });

  const parsed = bodySchema.safeParse(await request.json());
  if (!parsed.success) return NextResponse.json({ error: "..." }, { status: 400 });

  // delegate to use case or provider
  return NextResponse.json({ ... });
}
```

## Data fetching in pages

Server Components fetch via Prisma in page-level functions (e.g. `getFeedData`). Map DB records to domain types before passing to UI (`toNarrativeFeedItem`, `buildMoneyFlows`).

Filter by `ContextType` when the page is context-specific. Respect PF/PJ separation in queries.

## Open Finance endpoints

- `POST /api/open-finance/connect` — creates connect token; stub auto-creates demo connection
- `GET /api/cron/sync` — triggers `syncAllConnections` (open in dev without `CRON_SECRET`)
- `POST /api/webhooks/pluggy` — Pluggy events → `syncConnection`
